#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# coulomb_h1

#% text
# `coulomb_h1(l, eta, rho)` gives the outgoing Coulomb wave function `H+_l(eta, rho) = G_l(eta, rho) + i F_l(eta, rho)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `H+_l = e^(i theta) (-2 i rho)^(l + 1 + i eta) U(l + 1 + i eta, 2 l + 2, -2 i rho)` with `theta = rho - eta log(2 rho) - l pi/2 + sigma_l(eta)` and the Coulomb phase `sigma_l = (log_gamma(l + 1 + i eta) - log_gamma(l + 1 - i eta))/(2 i)` (DLMF 33.2.7, 33.2.10).

#% item
# At `eta = 0`, `H+_l(0, rho) = i rho h1_l(rho)`; `H+_0(0, rho) = e^(i rho)`.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
coulomb_h1(2, 0.2, 3.0)
#% output
#= 0.9784483839750212 + 0.8117976880895289im

#% cell
n(coulomb_h1(3, 2, 5), 25)
#% output
#= 2.04869471377719559294238463661 + 0.431315931140878690123879600042im

#% cell
coulomb_h1(1, 0.8, 5.0) - (coulomb_g(1, 0.8, 5.0) + im*coulomb_f(1, 0.8, 5.0))
#% output
#= 0.0 + 0.0im

#% cell
coulomb_h1(0, 0, r)
#% output
#= exp(im*r)

#% cell
n(coulomb_h1(11, -3, 70), 30)
#% output
#= -0.08638660006647463187750067853342391 - 0.9820310077292347389706320543648796im

